A place where Lojban deviated from logic, in that the "x" that is represent=
ed by=20
'ce'u' is a *bound* variable but without an explicit binder (historically=
=20
lambda), so, since there is only one word available for this role, it is ha=
rd to=20
tell whether the second 'ce'u' is another occurrence of the first (which is=
 what=20
is intended) or a new variable with a new (implicit) binder.  Subscripting =
the=20
'ce'u's would solve this problem, but no one seems to do it (and I am not e=
ven=20
sure 'ce'u' can take a subscript). I think the second interpretation is the=
=20
default one, but I couldn't find any discussion of how then to deal with th=
e=20
first case.



